      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Exarcheia"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The neighborhood is home to the National Technical University of Athens and Strefi Hill, anchoring its academic vibe.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        17
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Exarcheia"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "In 1973, the Athens Polytechnic uprising began in Exarcheia, a pivotal moment in Greece’s fight for democracy.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        22
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Exarcheia"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Exarcheia’s central square hosts one of Athens’ oldest summer cinemas, Vox, and the iconic Blue Building, a relic of inter‑war architecture.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        18
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Exarcheia"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The area is known for its vibrant anti‑capitalist graffiti, reflecting its long‑standing left‑wing activism.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        27
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Exarcheia"
    },
    {
